 "text": "Hi, how are you doing? Pick a spot that's flat, away from trees and close to water. Don't put it under a big rock or tree that could fall on it. Avoid under that tree. Even a little bit of root movement can wreck your tent. That's not good. If you can, move it away from it. Otherwise, spot it at a bigger angle, away from any dead branches. Keep at least ten feet away, and don't put anything ruggy or flammable near it. Some campsites have rules about fires too. Pretty much. Some tents also give you a list of areas to avoid and why, so read that before you pitch.",
